ions to **groups** (humans) and **roles** (workloads); avoid user-attached policies. Enforce **least privilege**, prefer federation and temporary credentials, and use tags or **permissions boundaries** to constrain scope. Review regularly to remove direct user policies and right-size access.\",\n  \"remediation_url\": \"https://hub.prowler.com/check/iam_policy_attached_only_to_group_or_roles\",\n  \"risk_details\": \"Directly attached user policies hinder centralized control and cause privilege creep. If a user is compromised, excessive rights enable data exposure, resource tampering, and lateral movement, harming **confidentiality** and **integrity**. Revocation is error-prone, weakening **separation of duties** and auditability.\",\n  \"referencias\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Remediation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://hub.prowler.com/check/iam_policy_attached_only_to_group_or_roles\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '2026-08-26 15:43:22', 'prowler_web', '2026-08-26 15:43:22', 1),
