ion of duties**:\\n- Replace `kms:*` with only needed actions scoped to specific key ARNs\\n- Apply policy conditions (e.g., `kms:ViaService`) and guardrails (permissions boundaries/SCPs)\\n- Monitor KMS usage and refine access based on activity\",\n  \"remediation_url\": \"https://hub.prowler.com/check/iam_policy_no_full_access_to_kms\",\n  \"risk_details\": \"Allowing `kms:*` lets principals decrypt data, change key policies, and disable or delete keys. Impact: **Confidentiality**-unauthorized decryption; **Integrity**-manipulation of cryptographic controls; **Availability**-data unreadable if keys are disabled/deleted. It can also enable privilege escalation.\",\n  \"referencias\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Remediation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://hub.prowler.com/check/iam_policy_no_full_access_to_kms\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '2026-08-26 15:43:22', 'prowler_web', '2026-08-26 15:43:22', 1),
