\n    \"FedRAMP-Low-Revision-4\": [\n      \"ac-2\"\n    ],\n    \"NIST-800-53-Revision-4\": [\n      \"ac_2_1\",\n      \"ac_2\"\n    ],\n    \"NIST-800-53-Revision-5\": [\n      \"ac_2_1\",\n      \"ac_3_3\",\n      \"ac_3_3_a\",\n      \"ac_3_3_b_1\",\n      \"ac_3_3_b_2\",\n      \"ac_3_3_b_3\",\n      \"ac_3_3_b_4\",\n      \"ac_3_3_b_5\",\n      \"ac_3_3_c\",\n      \"ac_3_4\",\n      \"ac_3_4_a\",\n      \"ac_3_4_b\",\n      \"ac_3_4_c\",\n      \"ac_3_4_d\",\n      \"ac_3_4_e\",\n      \"ac_3_8\",\n      \"ac_3_12_a\",\n      \"ac_3_13\",\n      \"ac_3_15_a\",\n      \"ac_3_15_b\",\n      \"ac_4_28\",\n      \"ac_24\",\n      \"cm_5_1_a\",\n      \"cm_6_a\",\n      \"cm_9_b\",\n      \"sc_23_3\"\n    ],\n    \"ProwlerThreatScore-1.0\": [\n      \"1.1.11\"\n    ],\n    \"KISA-ISMS-P-2023-korean\": [\n      \"2.7.2\",\n      \"2.10.2\"\n    ],\n    \"FedRAMP-20x-KSI-Low-25.05C\": [\n      \"ksi-iam\",\n      \"ksi-iam-07\"\n    ],\n    \"FedRamp-Moderate-Revision-4\": [\n      \"ac-2-1\",\n      \"ac-2-f\",\n      \"ac-2-j\"\n    ],\n    \"AWS-AI-Security-Framework-1.0\": [\n      \"AISF-IAM-03\"\n    ],\n    \"AWS-Foundational-Technical-Review\": [\n      \"IAM-002\",\n      \"IAM-0012\"\n    ],\n    \"AWS-Foundational-Security-Best-Practices\": [\n      \"IAM.3\"\n    ],\n    \"AWS-Well-Architected-Framework-Security-Pillar\": [\n      \"SEC02-BP02\",\n      \"SEC02-BP05\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"remediation\": \"Apply **least privilege** and limit static credentials:\\n- Rotate active access keys at or before `90 days`\\n- Prefer **IAM roles** with short-lived tokens\\n- Maintain only one active key during rotation; delete the old one\\n- Monitor `last_used` and remove dormant keys\\n- Automate alerts and periodic reviews of key age\",\n  \"remediation_url\": \"https://hub.prowler.com/check/iam_rotate_access_key_90_days\",\n  \"risk_details\": \"Long-lived access keys widen the attack window. If a key is leaked in code, logs, or tooling, lack of rotation keeps it valid for abuse, enabling unauthorized API calls, data exfiltration, and tampering. This degrades **confidentiality** and **integrity** and can impact **availability** and cost through destructive or excessive operations.\",\n  \"referencias\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Remediation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://hub.prowler.com/check/iam_rotate_access_key_90_days\"\n    }\n  ]\n}', '2026-08-26 15:43:22', 'prowler_web', '2026-08-26 15:43:22', 1),
